10266,0x2B43A18,HTTP Samples
10267,0x2B43A20,Texture Download
10268,0x2B43A28,"With HTTPManager.MaxConnectionPerServer you can control how many requests can be processed per server parallel.

Features demoed in this example:
-Parallel requests to the same server
-Controlling the parallelization
-Automatic Caching
-Create a Texture2D from the downloaded data"
10269,0x2B43A30,AssetBundle Download
10270,0x2B43A38,"A small example that shows a possible way to download an AssetBundle and load a resource from it.

Features demoed in this example:
-Using HTTPRequest without a callback
-Using HTTPRequest in a Coroutine
-Loading an AssetBundle from the downloaded bytes
-Automatic Caching"
10271,0x2B43A40,Large File Download
10272,0x2B43A48,"This example demonstrates how you can download a (large) file and continue the download after the connection is aborted.

Features demoed in this example:
-Setting up a streamed download
-How to access the downloaded data while the download is in progress
-Setting the HTTPRequest's StreamFragmentSize to controll the frequency and size of the fragments
-How to use the SetRangeHeader to continue a previously disconnected download
-How to disable the local, automatic caching"
10273,0x2B43A50,WebSocket Samples
10274,0x2B43A58,Echo
10275,0x2B43A60,"A WebSocket demonstration that connects to a WebSocket echo service.

Features demoed in this example:
-Basic usage of the WebSocket class"
10276,0x2B43A68,Socket.IO Samples
10277,0x2B43A70,Chat
10278,0x2B43A78,"This example uses the Socket.IO implementation to connect to the official Chat demo server(http://chat.socket.io/).

Features demoed in this example:
-Instantiating and setting up a SocketManager to connect to a Socket.IO server
-Changing SocketOptions property
-Subscribing to Socket.IO events
-Sending custom events to the server"
10279,0x2B43A80,WePlay
10280,0x2B43A88,"This example uses the Socket.IO implementation to connect to the official WePlay demo server(http://weplay.io/).

Features demoed in this example:
-Instantiating and setting up a SocketManager to connect to a Socket.IO server
-Subscribing to Socket.IO events
-Receiving binary data
-How to load a texture from the received binary data
-How to disable payload decoding for fine tune for some speed
-Sending custom events to the server"
10281,0x2B43A90,SignalR Core Samples
10282,0x2B43A98,Hub Sample
10283,0x2B43AA0,"This sample demonstrates most of the functionalities of the SignalR protocol:
-How to set up HubConnection to connect to the server
-Subscribing to server-callable function
-Calling client-callable function on the server
-Calling and handling streaming
"
10284,0x2B43AA8,SignalR Samples
10285,0x2B43AB0,Simple Streaming
10286,0x2B43AB8,"A very simple example of a background thread that broadcasts the server time to all connected clients every two seconds.

Features demoed in this example:
-Subscribing and handling non-hub messages"
10287,0x2B43AC0,Connection API
10288,0x2B43AC8,"Demonstrates all features of the lower-level connection API including starting and stopping, sending and receiving messages, and managing groups.

Features demoed in this example:
-Instantiating and setting up a SignalR Connection to connect to a SignalR server
-Changing the default Json encoder
-Subscribing to state changes
-Receiving and handling of non-hub messages
-Sending non-hub messages
-Managing groups"
10289,0x2B43AD0,Connection Status
10290,0x2B43AD8,"Demonstrates how to handle the events that are raised when connections connect, reconnect and disconnect from the Hub API.

Features demoed in this example:
-Connecting to a Hub
-Setting up a callback for Hub events
-Handling server-sent method call requests
-Calling a Hub-method on the server-side
-Opening and closing the SignalR Connection"
10291,0x2B43AE0,Demo Hub
10292,0x2B43AE8,"A contrived example that exploits every feature of the Hub API.

Features demoed in this example:
-Creating and using wrapper Hub classes to encapsulate hub functions and events
-Handling long running server-side functions by handling progress messages
-Groups
-Handling server-side functions with return value
-Handling server-side functions throwing Exceptions
-Calling server-side functions with complex type parameters
-Calling server-side functions with array parameters
-Calling overloaded server-side functions
-Changing Hub states
-Receiving and handling hub state changes
-Calling server-side functions implemented in VB .NET"
10293,0x2B43AF0,Authentication
10294,0x2B43AF8,"Demonstrates how to use the authorization features of the Hub API to restrict certain Hubs and methods to specific users.

Features demoed in this example:
-Creating and using wrapper Hub classes to encapsulate hub functions and events
-Create and use a Header-based authenticator to access protected APIs
-SignalR over HTTPS"
10295,0x2B43B00,Plugin Samples
10296,0x2B43B08,Cache Maintenance
10297,0x2B43B10,"With this demo you can see how you can use the HTTPCacheService's BeginMaintainence function to delete too old cached entities and keep the cache size under a specified value.

Features demoed in this example:
-How to set up a HTTPCacheMaintananceParams
-How to call the BeginMaintainence function"
